WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
The year is 632.

2
00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:04.470
The Prophet Muhammad dies.

3
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.770
His companions remember
his words and teach them.

4
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.780
Over the next century, reports multiply.

5
00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:15.010
Some are invented: for
politics, for rival sects,

6
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.800
even out of piety.

7
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.710
In the 9th century, a scholar called
al-Bukhari keeps only the reports he judges

8
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:22.790
sound.

9
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:27.140
So how do Muslims decide whether
the Prophet really said something?

10
00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:30.120
In this mission, you'll see
how the Prophet's example,

11
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.210
the Sunnah, is carried by
single reports called hadiths.

12
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.080
Then you'll read why the Qur'an tells
Muslims to follow the Prophet's example.

13
00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:43.830
Your mission: find out how Muslims decide
whether a saying really comes from the

14
00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:44.510
Prophet.
